line	
line	<str>Search the bookcase in the south-east corner and read Varmen's notes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Curator Haig Halen in the Varrock Museum about the statuette. ( if Bone Voyage is started)</str>
line	
line	<str>Pickpocket him for the display cabinet key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs, and open the second-most western case in the northern-most row. You will get a statuette.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the Kharidian Desert (fairy ring DLQ), or teleport to Eagle's Eyrie with Necklace of passage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the ruins of Uzer where you started the quest and again go down the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>In the centre of the room will be four alcoves. Place the statuette in the empty one.</str>
line	
line	<str>Turn the statues until they all point north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go north, through the double doors.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Optional: Use your chisel and hammer on the throne for 2 sapphires, emeralds, and rubies.</col>
step	22	-	Quick guide step 22
line	<str>Travel to the Ruins of Uzer via the necklace of passage teleport to Eagle's Eyrie and run south-east. You can alternatively use a fairy ring (DLQ) and go north-east.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up and read the Letter west of the broken clay golem</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the golem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use four soft clay on the golem. If you chose to bring a pickaxe and a bracelet of clay, clay rocks can be found to the north-west, near the shore. The phoenix can be found there as well.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the golem again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick a black mushroom near the stairs east of the golem before heading down (or downstairs at your right).</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs in the ruins.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the strange implement from the north-western room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to the Golem again</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the most north-eastern part of the Digsite, near the large buried skeleton, and talk to Elissa. (make sure to read the letter if no 3rd option is seen)</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the Exam Centre just south of the Digsite.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the bookcase in the south-east corner and read Varmen's notes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Curator Haig Halen in the Varrock Museum about the statuette. ( if Bone Voyage is started)</str>
line	
line	<str>Pickpocket him for the display cabinet key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs, and open the second-most western case in the northern-most row. You will get a statuette.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the Kharidian Desert (fairy ring DLQ), or teleport to Eagle's Eyrie with Necklace of passage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the ruins of Uzer where you started the quest and again go down the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>In the centre of the room will be four alcoves. Place the statuette in the empty one.</str>
line	
line	<str>Turn the statues until they all point north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go north, through the double doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Optional: Use your chisel and hammer on the throne for 2 sapphires, emeralds, and rubies.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Otherwise, immediately go back through the south portal.</col>
